/*
 * Larger text for leader- and public-facing screens (older leaders with reading
 * difficulties — Peter, 2026-10-14). Put the `large-text` class on a wrapper and
 * every Tailwind text size inside it goes up by roughly 4px. This is deliberately
 * plain, UNLAYERED CSS: unlayered rules beat Tailwind's layered utilities, so it
 * wins over the element's own `text-sm` (and over `sm:text-…` variants) without
 * editing hundreds of class lists. Not applied to /admin (dense tables), the
 * header/bottom-nav chrome, or the email/2FA setup screens (those already use
